# Each upstream revision is registered once, and no list is kept of
# where it is restated.
#
# A revision cannot be stated only once — a Cargo manifest reads no
# file, a captured fixture carries what it was captured against, a
# third-party notice must name what it notices. What can be avoided is
# a hand-maintained register of those sites, because a site nobody
# remembered to add is a site the check passes over in silence, which
# is how a gate like this usually stops meaning anything.
#
# So the check finds rather than enumerates: every Cargo dependency's
# revision, wherever the manifest lives, and every file that says for
# itself that it restates a pin. An upstream nothing depends on fails
# too, so an entry cannot linger past its dependant.

# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/upstream-pins.py %S/../.. | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: {{[0-9]+}} statements agree with 2 registered upstreams
